      "content": "To calculate the straight-line depreciation, subtract the salvage value ($5,000) from your initial cost ($85,000) to get a depreciable base of $80,000. Divide this amount by the machine's 10-year useful life, resulting in an annual depreciation expense of $8,000. You can record this $8,000 as an expense each year until the end of the tenth year. This method evenly spreads the cost over the asset's life, making it simple for accurate year-end reporting.",
