      "role": "user",
      "content": "Got it. So it's basically just a flat rate. I was thinking about looking into other methods like accelerated depreciation just to see if they'd be better for tax purposes, though. In your professional opinion, is there a big downside to just sticking with the straightforward approach for something like this? Like, am I missing out on anything significant by not being more \"complex\" with it?",
