      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Sticking with straight-line depreciation has no significant downsides for most small-to-medium businesses, as it provides consistency and simplifies tax reporting without risking penalties. Accelerated methods might temporarily lower your taxable income more aggressively, but they complicate calculations and often require stricter documentation to justify higher early-year deductions. Given your equipment's long 10-year life, the complexity of switching methods rarely outweighs the benefits of a stable, predictable schedule. You are not missing out on critical tax savings, but the savings from acceleration are often modest for assets with steady utility over time.",
